    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d616">

                <pb facs="0845" n="749" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg749"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Day to Mr.
                            Woodford.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-04-10T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 10,
                                1898—About 6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>The Spanish minister to-day informed me that authority had been given General
                    Blanco to proclaim suspension of hostilities, and thereupon invited, on
                    General’s behalf, indication of nature and scope of such proclamation. Spanish
                    minister had been answered that the President must decline to make further
                    suggestions than those heretofore made know through you and through Spanish
                    minister here, but that in sending in his message to-morrow the President will
                    acquaint Congress with this latest communication of the Spanish Government and
                    add any further information which Minister Polo may be in a position to furnish
                    in regard to the nature and terms of General Blanco’s action under the
                    authorization so given him. The above is sent for your information. Your
                    personal, No. 66, just received and fully noted.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Day.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
